prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "add", "docs/project/03-domain/01-domain-model.md", "docs/project/03-domain/02-ubiquitous-language.md", "docs/project/04-design/05-data-model.md"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "switch"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "merge"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "merge-tree", "--write-tree", "origin/main", "HEAD"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "gh pr edit 24 --body $'## What does this PR do and why?\\n\\nAligns the domain model and data model around the review findings for Payment, Organization, Notification, Sponsorship, and relationship documentation. It also resolves the current conflicts with latest `main` by keeping the domain-level `type + single typed id` value object model and flattening those value objects only in the write model.\\n\\n- Adds missing domain enum definitions for referenced value sets.\\n- Makes Payment payer/payee, processor provider, method type, and payment type explicit in the domain model.\\n- Adds matching data model CHECK constraints for Payment payer/payee, Payment provider, payment method type, payment target/type consistency, Sponsorship ended reason, and Notification type.\\n- Adds Organization membership summary columns and active membership status modeling.\\n- Adds missing relationship documentation and fixes the Chat membership ERD name.\\n- Preserves `FollowTarget`, `EventHost`, `EventSeriesOwner`, `Sponsor` / `Sponsee`, `PaymentPayer` / `PaymentPayee`, `PaymentMethodOwner`, and `RevenueHost` as typed value objects in the domain model.\\n\\n## References\\n\\nN/A\\n\\n## Screenshots or screen recordings\\n\\nN/A. Documentation-only change.\\n\\n## How to set up and validate locally\\n\\n1. Run `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`.\\n1. Run `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD` and confirm it exits with 0.\\n1. Confirm old names and obsolete constraints are gone:\\n   `PaymentProvider`, `SOCIAL_CHAT_PARTICIPANTS`, `removed_at`, and `provider CHECK (provider IN (\\'stripe\\', \\'apple_pay\\', \\'google_pay\\'))`.\\n1. Confirm new constraints and model terms are present:\\n   `payment_payer_exactly_one`, `payment_payee_exactly_one`, `payment_target_matches_type`, `NotificationType`, `PaymentProcessorProvider`, and `SOCIAL_CHAT_MEMBERSHIPS`.\\n'"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "merge-tree"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh", "pr", "merge"], decision="allow")
